ss, long\u2011duration flights calmly; \u2013 Strong positive teamwork evidence for any other candidate; \u2013 Evidence that A\u2019s attitude materially impairs crew cooperation; \u2013 Evidence of critical technical or decision\u2011making flaws in A.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate A\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. We must evaluate candidates based on given attributes. Agent 2's own info includes all listed attributes? The prompt says \"Information available to you:\" list includes many facts about each candidate. So agent_2 has all those facts. Need to weigh them.\n\nLet's list positives and negatives:\n\nCandidate A:\nPositives: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities.\nNegatives: regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nCandidate B:\nPositives: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills.\nNegatives: relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues.\n\nCandidate C:\nPositives: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology.\nNegatives: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education.\n\nCandidate D:\nPositives: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously.\nNegatives: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nNow evaluate against criteria: reliability/responsibility, technical competence, calmness/pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nCandidate A: strong technical (spatial vision, complex connections), leadership, anticipates danger (reliability). Negatives: show-off (could affect teamwork), not open to new ideas (could hinder development). No explicit calmness under pressure info. Might be okay